-- s 1072(2): a document not properly delivered is treated as not delivered, subject to section 1073
#ASSERT `s 1072(2) the document is treated as not having been delivered` (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1072(2) the document is treated as not having been delivered` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1072(2) the document is treated as not having been delivered` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1072(2) the document is treated as not having been delivered` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1072(2) the document is treated as not having been delivered` NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 1073(1) and (2): the registrar may accept a document that does not comply; one accepted is treated as received for section 1077
#ASSERT `s 1073(1) the registrar may accept and register the document` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1073(1) the registrar may accept and register the document` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1073(2) the document is treated as received by the registrar for the purposes of section 1077` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1073(2) the document is treated as received by the registrar for the purposes of section 1077` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 1073(3): no objection may be taken, on the ground that the requirements were not met, to the legal consequences of acceptance
#ASSERT `s 1073(3) an objection may be taken on that ground` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1073(3) an objection may be taken on that ground` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1073(3) an objection may be taken on that ground` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1073(3) an objection may be taken on that ground` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 1073(4): acceptance does not affect the continuing obligation; as to liability it is subject to what follows; another matter is not decided
#ASSERT `s 1073(4) the acceptance of the document affects the matter` `s 1073(4)(a) the continuing obligation to comply with the requirements for proper delivery` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1073(4) the acceptance of the document affects the matter` `s 1073(4)(b) any liability for failure to comply with those requirements` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1073(4) the acceptance of the document affects the matter` `s 1073(4) another matter` EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 1073(5) and (6): accepted on 1 March 2025; the period after counts as default for neither section 453 nor a daily default fine, unless a notice under section 1094A(1) issued on 1 June 2025 is not complied with within 14 days (the period ends on 15 June 2025); then default after 15 June counts
